From ae9c9b52690580a6a7e0843bee58029cb806b6c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: icanc0 <ai7@vincentxie.net>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:30:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P7: scaffold kicad-cli daemon subcommand (start/stop/status)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New kicad/cli/command_daemon.{h,cpp} adds `kicad-cli daemon` with
start/stop/status children. All three currently print 'not yet
implemented' and exit non-zero — this patch lands only the argparse
plumbing and CMakeLists.txt entry, so subsequent patches can fill in
the Unix-socket server, request framing, dispatcher, and BOARD cache
without also having to touch the top-level kicad_cli.cpp.

See analysis/02-daemon-mode-design.md in the kicad-perf repo for the
full plan (~500 LOC across ~6 files). Expected impact: 10-60× speedup
on CI-shaped workflows that call kicad-cli many times against the same
board.
---
 kicad/CMakeLists.txt         |   1 +
 kicad/cli/command_daemon.cpp | 105 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 kicad/cli/command_daemon.h   |  78 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 kicad/kicad_cli.cpp          |  13 +++++
 4 files changed, 197 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 kicad/cli/command_daemon.cpp
 create mode 100644 kicad/cli/command_daemon.h

diff --git a/kicad/CMakeLists.txt b/kicad/CMakeLists.txt
index 68fdbbb8..626657d1 100644
--- a/kicad/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/kicad/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@ set( KICAD_CLI_SRCS
     cli/command_gerber_convert_png.cpp
     cli/command_gerber_diff.cpp
     cli/command_version.cpp
+    cli/command_daemon.cpp
 
     jobs_runner.cpp
     )
